          "python",
          "=== Implicit Feedback Conversion ===\n\nInteraction counts (User 1):\n  [10, 8, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 5, 0]\n\nBinary preferences (User 1):\n  [1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0]\n\nConfidence scores (alpha=0.5, User 1):\n  [6.0, 5.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.5, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 3.5, 1.0]\n\n--- Key Insight ---\nItem_3: preference=0, confidence=1.0 (low confidence it's disliked)\nItem_1: preference=1, confidence=6.0 (high confidence it's liked)\nUnobserved items are NOT 'disliked' - we just don't know yet\n\n=== Comparison: Explicit vs Implicit ===\n           Aspect                Explicit                       Implicit\nData availability     Very sparse (1-5%)               Dense (30-60%)\n   Signal clarity      Clear preference           Ambiguous confidence\n  Absence meaning               Unknown           Unknown (NOT dislike)\n            Scale       Ordinal (1-5)            Continuous counts\n      Noise level                 Low                           High\n  Typical density          <5% filled              30-60% non-zero"
